        "text": "This dynamic. Expensive to produce, cheap to verify is some of the game theory that makes blockchain systems viable. You'll be out of pocket if you produce an invalid block, as the other nodes will immediately reject it. Proof of work was the first consensus mechanism to surface and remains important. This process of using proof of work to solve a block is called mining, and nodes that participate in mining are called miners. We call them miners because they're working to extract a reward from the protocol. Despite proof of work strength for preventing system abuses with a high level of security, it has some limitations. For one thing, when the network becomes larger, it requires expensive equipment and high energy usage.",
